[size=5][b]SmoothCam - UE4SS[/b][/size]
[i]A smoother third-person camera: it trails your character instead of being bolted to it.[/i]

The game's camera follows your character almost rigidly, so every step, stop and jump lands on the view at once. With this mod the camera trails a little behind and catches up smoothly, horizontally and vertically, each at its own rate. Turning the camera stays instant: only the follow lags, so aiming and looking around feel exactly as before. Near walls the camera still pulls in the way the game's does, and after a cutscene, a load or a teleport it snaps back to your character instead of gliding across the map.

It also sets where the camera sits, separately for each situation: exploring, sprinting, combat and focus, aiming, and claw ride and anti-grav. For each one you choose the distance, height, shoulder offset and field of view. Everything is set in an ini file, or from an in-game page if you also run [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/271]Dawnwalker Mod Menu[/url].

[size=4][b]Presets and keys[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]O[/font]: switch the smooth follow on and off.
[*][font=Courier New]V[/font]: cycle presets. [b]Tight[/b] barely trails. [b]Balanced[/b] is a clear trail that settles fast (the default). [b]Cinematic[/b] is a heavy, slow trail with smoothed turning. Six slots of your own come after them, once you save them.
[*][font=Courier New]N[/font]: move the camera to the other shoulder. It glides across in half a second.
[/list]
A short banner at the top of the screen names the preset, or says On or Off. Quick presses show one banner with the last name. A preset carries the follow feel only (follow speeds, lag limits, turning); camera position is left as you set it. All three keys can be changed in the ini.

[size=4][b]Performance[/b][/size]
The camera math runs once per frame inside the game's camera update and takes 3.3 to 3.6 microseconds, measured at 47 and 57 fps, standing and moving. That is about 0.02 % of a 21 ms frame. A whole-frame A/B with UEBench (four 20-second captures, alternating on and off at the same spot) found no measurable frame-time difference: median frame times of 21.19 ms on and 21.22 ms off, a gap smaller than the spread between two captures in the same state, and no stutters either way.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/18]UE4SS for Dawnwalker[/url] by Vercadi, file [font=Courier New]Dawnwalker-UE4SS-v1.2.1-rc6-build25232147[/font] (version 1.3 on that page). Required: the DLL is built against UE4SS commit 97b7e501, the base of that loader, and C++ mods only load on the UE4SS they were built for.
[*]The Steam version of the game, build 25232147.
[*]Optional: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/271]Dawnwalker Mod Menu[/url] for the in-game settings page.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
Close the game first. Extract the archive into the folder that contains the [i]ue4ss[/i] folder and [font=Courier New]Dawnwalker.exe[/font]:
[code]<Steam library>\steamapps\common\The Blood of Dawnwalker\Dawnwalker\Binaries\Win64[/code]
The archive contains the path, so the mod lands in [font=Courier New]ue4ss\Mods\DWSmoothCam[/font]. No [font=Courier New]mods.txt[/font] edit: [font=Courier New]enabled.txt[/font] in the mod folder enables it. [font=Courier New]UE4SS.log[/font] shows this on load:
[code][DWSmoothCam] v0.7.4 loaded, on
[DWSmoothCam] GetCameraView hooked (slot 214)[/code]

Uninstall: close the game and delete [font=Courier New]ue4ss\Mods\DWSmoothCam[/font]. Nothing is written to save games; the camera changes live in memory and are gone on the next launch.

[size=4][b]Dawnwalker Mod Menu page[/b][/size] (optional)
With [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/271]Dawnwalker Mod Menu[/url] installed, SmoothCam gets its own page under Mod Settings, in the main menu and in the pause menu. It covers every setting except the three key bindings, and it loads and saves presets. Press Apply and the change takes effect within a quarter second, with no restart.

Without the Mod Menu, edit [font=Courier New]scripts\config\smoothcam.ini[/font] in the mod folder. Changes apply within a quarter second while the game runs; save the file and look back at the game. Key bindings are read when the game starts.

[size=4][b]Known limits[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Supports Steam build 25232147 only. On any other build the mod refuses to hook the camera and stays inactive. [font=Courier New]UE4SS.log[/font] says so: [font=Courier New]unsupported game build, mod inactive[/font].
[*]After loading a preset from the Mod Menu, reopen the SmoothCam page before changing anything else. The mod writes the preset into the ini, and the menu refuses an Apply on a page whose file changed since it opened.
[*][font=Courier New]V[/font] and [font=Courier New]N[/font] are ignored while the game is paused, including with the Mod Menu open. [font=Courier New]O[/font] works at any time.
[*]Smoothed turning (on in Cinematic, off otherwise) adds a little delay to aiming.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Conflicts with any other mod that replaces the third-person camera. Run one or the other.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/350]FreeCam - UE4SS[/url] ([font=Courier New]F7[/font]) works alongside it. When you leave the free camera, the game camera snaps back to your character.
[*]Keys: SmoothCam uses [font=Courier New]O[/font], [font=Courier New]V[/font] and [font=Courier New]N[/font], all unbound in this game. P, F5 and F9 are used by the game.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size] ([font=Courier New]scripts\config\smoothcam.ini[/font] in the mod folder)
[spoiler]
[b]Keys[/b] (read at game start; any UE4SS key name)
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]toggle_key = O[/font], [font=Courier New]preset_key = V[/font], [font=Courier New]shoulder_key = N[/font]
[/list]
[b]Follow[/b] (what presets carry)
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]enabled = 1[/font]: 0 turns the smooth follow off. Camera position has its own switch.
[*][font=Courier New]follow_rate_h = 8[/font], [font=Courier New]follow_rate_v = 10[/font]: catch-up rate per second, horizontal and vertical. Higher is tighter.
[*][font=Courier New]curve_h = 2[/font], [font=Courier New]curve_v = 0[/font]: 0 constant, 1 linear, 2 smoothstep, 3 ease in-out. The curves start gently and reach full rate at [font=Courier New]catchup_distance = 150[/font] cm; [font=Courier New]min_rate_scale = 0.35[/font] is the rate at zero lag.
[*][font=Courier New]max_lag_h = 70[/font], [font=Courier New]max_lag_v = 50[/font]: the furthest the camera may fall behind, in cm.
[*][font=Courier New]soft_leash = 1[/font]: eases into the lag limit instead of stopping hard at it.
[*][font=Courier New]rotation_smoothing = 0[/font], [font=Courier New]rotation_rate = 20[/font]: smooth turning too, and how fast it catches up.
[*][font=Courier New]wall_clamp = 1[/font]: keeps the smoothed camera in front of walls the game pulled its camera in for.
[/list]
[b]Safety and display[/b]
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]reset_distance = 500[/font]: cm moved in one frame that counts as a teleport and snaps the camera.
[*][font=Courier New]reset_gap = 0.25[/font]: seconds without camera updates (cutscene, free camera, load) before a snap.
[*][font=Courier New]show_banner = 1[/font]: the preset and on/off banner.
[*][font=Courier New]log_stats = 0[/font]: 1 writes smoothing statistics and the per-frame cost to [font=Courier New]UE4SS.log[/font] every 5 seconds.
[/list]
[b]Camera position[/b] (100 / 0 / 0 / 0 is the game as shipped)
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]camera_tuning = 1[/font]: 0 puts every camera mode back as the game ships it.
[*]Per group, with the prefix [font=Courier New]exploration_[/font], [font=Courier New]sprint_[/font], [font=Courier New]combat_[/font], [font=Courier New]aiming_[/font] or [font=Courier New]traversal_[/font]: [font=Courier New]distance[/font] (% of the game's, 50 to 250), [font=Courier New]height[/font] (cm), [font=Courier New]shoulder[/font] (cm further out; centred cameras stay centred; not for traversal), [font=Courier New]fov[/font] (degrees added).
[*][font=Courier New]game_lag_scale = 1[/font]: multiplies the game's own camera lag speeds. Higher makes the game's part tighter.
[*][font=Courier New]shoulder_swap = 0[/font]: 1 is the other shoulder. [font=Courier New]N[/font] switches it.
[*][font=Courier New]position_transition = 0.5[/font]: seconds a position change or shoulder swap glides over. 0 snaps.
[*][font=Courier New]pitch_min = -60[/font], [font=Courier New]pitch_max = 40[/font]: look down and up limits while exploring, sprinting and in focus. Aiming and combat already allow -89 / 89.
[/list]
[b]Menu actions[/b]: [font=Courier New]preset_load[/font] (101 Tight, 102 Balanced, 103 Cinematic, 1 to 6 a slot) and [font=Courier New]preset_save[/font] (1 to 6). The mod runs them and sets them back to 0. Saved slots go to [font=Courier New]scripts\config\presets.ini[/font], which the mod creates.
[/spoiler]

[size=4][b]Credits[/b][/size]
Built on [url=https://github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS]UE4SS[/url] by the UE4SS-RE team (MIT). Requires [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thebloodofdawnwalker/mods/18]Vercadi's UE4SS build[/url] for this game. GPL-3.0-or-later, included in the archive.
